# rfc-007-comment-feedback.mdc

## Title
RFC 007 – Comment & Feedback System

## Summary
This RFC defines the design and implementation of a comment and feedback system for videos. Users will be able to write comments, provide structured feedback, and interact with video content more effectively.

---

## Goals
- Allow users to write comments under videos
- Enable marking feedback as "useful", "incomplete", or "incorrect"
- Admins and Team Leads can delete inappropriate comments

## Database Tables
### `comments`
| Field         | Type      | Description                          |
|---------------|-----------|--------------------------------------|
| id            | uuid      | Primary key                          |
| user_id       | uuid      | FK to `profiles`                     |
| video_id      | uuid      | FK to `videos`                       |
| content       | text      | Comment body                         |
| feedback_type | text      | ENUM: 'useful', 'incomplete', 'incorrect' (nullable) |
| created_at    | timestamp | Created time                         |

## UI Implementation
- Comments listed under each video detail page
- Comment input box for logged-in users
- Radio button or dropdown for selecting feedback type
- Admin/Team Lead sees delete button on each comment

## Role Permissions
| Role        | Permissions                          |
|-------------|---------------------------------------|
| Admin       | View, create, delete all comments     |
| Team Lead   | View, create, delete within team      |
| User        | View and create own comments          |
| Guest       | ❌ No access to commenting             |

## Validation Rules
- Comment content must be 3+ characters
- One feedback_type per comment (optional)
- Max comment length: 1000 characters

## Timeline
**Sprint 7**
- Create `comments` table
- Build comment UI component
- Integrate feedback selection dropdown
- Add moderation (delete button) logic for authorized users

